  ⭐⭐ DSC/UNC collapses 33.78% at t=0 -> 0.13%, its minimum, at t=250. ⇒ the tail failure
     is a DISCRIMINATION failure, not a calibration one: the probabilities up there
     carry almost no information about WHICH cells exceed the threshold.
  ⛔ That is neither 'too high' nor 'too low'. It is a third thing.

